1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,466
A workflow can react when content changes, and change content in return.

2
00:00:05,466 --> 00:00:10,104
In this video, we'll build one that creates an announcement when an article

3
00:00:10,104 --> 00:00:13,310
is published, fills in its body, and publishes it.

4
00:00:17,910 --> 00:00:23,436
With the Workflows feature enabled, the Contents module adds activities for content.

5
00:00:23,436 --> 00:00:28,286
Events start a workflow when a content item is created, updated, saved as

6
00:00:28,286 --> 00:00:31,970
a draft, published, unpublished, deleted or versioned.

7
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:36,047
A content handler raises each event with two inputs:

8
00:00:36,047 --> 00:00:40,463
the Content Item, and a Content Event that names the event, the content

9
00:00:40,463 --> 00:00:41,782
type and the ids.

10
00:00:41,782 --> 00:00:45,510
The workflow is correlated with the id of the content item.

11
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:51,626
Tasks create, retrieve, update, publish, unpublish and delete content items.

12
00:00:51,626 --> 00:00:56,666
Each ends with outcomes you connect to the next activity, such as Done,

13
00:00:56,666 --> 00:00:58,760
Failed, Published or Noop.

14
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:06,013
In Design, Workflows, choose Create Workflow.

15
00:01:06,013 --> 00:01:10,588
A workflow only needs a name, so call it Announce published articles, and

16
00:01:10,588 --> 00:01:13,020
select Create and open the designer.

17
00:01:14,617 --> 00:01:18,256
An empty workflow offers the events that usually start one.

18
00:01:18,256 --> 00:01:20,327
Choose Content Published Event.

19
00:01:20,327 --> 00:01:25,197
It becomes the start activity, and its settings open at the bottom of the canvas.

20
00:01:25,672 --> 00:01:29,100
In Content Types, search for Article and select it.

21
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:34,092
With nothing selected, the event starts the workflow for content of any type.

22
00:01:38,344 --> 00:01:42,402
Point at the Done outcome and click the plus that appears, search for

23
00:01:42,402 --> 00:01:45,270
Create Content, and choose Create Content Task.

24
00:01:45,270 --> 00:01:48,354
It is added after the event, and its settings open.

25
00:01:48,818 --> 00:01:52,027
Content Type lists the content types of the site.

26
00:01:52,027 --> 00:01:53,544
Choose Announcement.

27
00:01:53,544 --> 00:01:58,678
Publish stays unchecked, so the task saves a draft instead of publishing the item.

28
00:01:59,138 --> 00:02:03,243
Content Properties takes JSON for the parts and fields of the item.

29
00:02:03,243 --> 00:02:08,808
Liquid reads the workflow, so the title of the announcement follows the title of the article.

30
00:02:10,408 --> 00:02:13,924
The task renders Content Properties as Liquid first.

31
00:02:13,924 --> 00:02:19,198
Liquid output is encoded, so a quotation mark in a title does not break the JSON.

32
00:02:19,198 --> 00:02:22,168
The JSON is then merged into an empty item.

33
00:02:22,918 --> 00:02:26,476
If the item is valid, the task creates it and takes Done.

34
00:02:26,476 --> 00:02:31,728
If it is not, the task takes Failed, and the validation result becomes the last result.

35
00:02:35,994 --> 00:02:42,057
Point at the Done outcome, click the plus that appears, and choose Update Content Task.

36
00:02:42,057 --> 00:02:48,184
Content Item ID takes a JavaScript expression that returns the id of the item to update.

37
00:02:48,637 --> 00:02:54,007
Type an expression that returns the id of the item the Create Content Task made.

38
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:59,127
The Available data tab lists expressions like it for every earlier activity.

39
00:02:59,613 --> 00:03:03,064
Content Properties merges more JSON into the draft.

40
00:03:03,064 --> 00:03:07,302
Here it sets the body, and Liquid reads the content type and the

41
00:03:07,302 --> 00:03:08,937
title of the article.

42
00:03:08,937 --> 00:03:10,753
Publish stays unchecked.

43
00:03:12,353 --> 00:03:17,320
Update Content Task loads the draft of that item, merges the JSON into

44
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:20,195
it, validates it, and saves the draft.

45
00:03:20,195 --> 00:03:23,463
Objects are merged, and arrays are replaced.

46
00:03:24,213 --> 00:03:25,785
There is no fallback:

47
00:03:25,785 --> 00:03:30,735
without a Content Item ID, the task throws, and by default the instance faults.

48
00:03:30,735 --> 00:03:34,753
Check Publish to publish the update, instead of saving a draft.

49
00:03:39,035 --> 00:03:41,838
Add a Publish Content Task after Done.

50
00:03:41,838 --> 00:03:46,935
Its Expression returns the content item to publish, or the id of the item.

51
00:03:47,966 --> 00:03:52,797
Enter an expression for the property named Content Item, which the Create Content

52
00:03:52,797 --> 00:03:56,296
Task and the Update Content Task set to the announcement.

53
00:03:57,896 --> 00:04:02,078
With an empty Expression, the task looks for an input named Content Item,

54
00:04:02,078 --> 00:04:03,931
then a property of that name.

55
00:04:03,931 --> 00:04:07,902
A content event sets the input to the item that started the workflow,

56
00:04:07,902 --> 00:04:10,496
so the expression selects the announcement.

57
00:04:11,246 --> 00:04:16,612
Publish Content Task takes Published after publishing a draft, and Noop when the

58
00:04:16,612 --> 00:04:18,109
item has no draft.

59
00:04:18,109 --> 00:04:23,226
Unpublish Content Task and Delete Content Task find their item the same way.

60
00:04:27,483 --> 00:04:29,946
Click Publish to publish the workflow.

61
00:04:29,946 --> 00:04:33,919
The designer saves a draft as you work, and a draft does not run:

62
00:04:33,919 --> 00:04:36,773
new instances start on the published version.

63
00:04:37,255 --> 00:04:39,232
Let's publish an article.

64
00:04:39,232 --> 00:04:42,485
Create one, enter a title, and click Publish.

65
00:04:49,965 --> 00:04:53,831
In Content Items, the Announcement is listed as published.

66
00:04:53,831 --> 00:04:54,676
Open it:

67
00:04:54,676 --> 00:04:59,085
its title and its body were built from the article by the workflow.

68
00:05:03,285 --> 00:05:05,481
Tasks guard against infinite loops.

69
00:05:05,481 --> 00:05:09,551
A task that would raise again the event that started the workflow, for

70
00:05:09,551 --> 00:05:13,407
the same content type, throws, and by default the instance faults.

71
00:05:13,407 --> 00:05:16,245
That is why the announcement is not an Article.

72
00:05:16,995 --> 00:05:19,535
Invalid content is not an exception:

73
00:05:19,535 --> 00:05:25,886
Create Content Task and Update Content Task take Failed, which you can connect to another activity.

74
00:05:25,886 --> 00:05:29,575
Publish Content Task takes Noop when there is no draft.

75
00:05:33,775 --> 00:05:39,435
Export downloads the published workflow in a package whose recipe has a WorkflowType step.

76
00:05:39,435 --> 00:05:44,034
Each activity is a record with its type and properties, and a transition

77
00:05:44,034 --> 00:05:47,335
names the outcome that leads to the next activity.

78
00:05:49,335 --> 00:05:53,451
That is how a workflow creates, updates and publishes content:

79
00:05:53,451 --> 00:05:59,141
a content event, expressions that point at the item, and Liquid and JSON for its values.

80
00:05:59,141 --> 00:06:00,715
Thanks for watching.

